{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3831","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3831","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3831\",\"parent_revision\":\"96ee3ec88553d35a01f339055c8f22ac903a0464e33740795f129047a0ff814e\",\"root_revision\":\"96ee3ec88553d35a01f339055c8f22ac903a0464e33740795f129047a0ff814e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA section name written through backlog_groom is stored under a key that discards case and punctuation, so the name it reads back under is not the name that was written. 'RFC-2119 Notes' reads back as 'Rfc 2119 Notes'; 'Cost & Latency' as 'Cost Latency'; 'Diffusion/Images' as 'Diffusion Images'.\\n\\nNothing is lost and no caller is misled today. The warning emitted on the write names the retrievable spelling, and tests/test_section_registry.py pins that round trip. This item is only about the caller's own spelling not surviving.\\n\\nDistinct from #2966 and #2968, which are both about a key DIVERGING across a render+parse round trip: #2966 for exotic Unicode where title() and lower() are not mutual inverses, #2968 for literal underscores colliding with space substitution. This is not a divergence. The loss is deterministic, happens on the first write, and applies to ordinary ASCII. The key is stable; it just is not the caller's name.\\n\\nEstablished while fixing the write message (branch fix/message-audit-remainder): heading_to_unknown_key lowercases before building the key, so the rebuilt heading's casing never affects round-trip stability with GitHub. The mangling is therefore not required by the round trip.\\n\\nThe design question to answer: keeping the caller's spelling means storing a display name alongside the key. Decide whether that is worth the second field, or whether naming the retrievable spelling in the message is the whole fix.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"199c3688d0f073d7cc6f753237498b041b3d8593428c6da40a64f27d7330c800\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCDyCA\"}"}